          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮೈತ್ರಿ — maitri — \"an alliance; friendship\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಎರಡು ಊರುಗಳ ನಡುವೆ ಹಳೆಯ ಮೈತ್ರಿ ಇದೆ. eraḍu ūrugaḷa naḍuve haḷeya maitri ide. There is an old friendship between the two towns."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Formal; between groups or countries."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮೈತ್ರಿ (maitri) is borrowed from Sanskrit maitrī, \"friendship, goodwill\" (Monier-Williams), from mitra, \"a friend\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
